.TH MONGOOSE 1 "September 2026" "mongoose 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mongoose \- single-host NFS-to-NFS data mover with incremental resync
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mongoose
.RI [ \-v | \-vv ]
.B prepare
.BI \-\-src " URL"
.BI \-\-dst " URL"
.BI \-\-work\-dir " DIR"
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B mongoose
.RI [ \-v | \-vv ]
.B copy
.BI \-\-work\-dir " DIR"
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B mongoose
.RI [ \-v | \-vv ]
.B run
.BI \-\-src " URL"
.BI \-\-dst " URL"
.BI \-\-work\-dir " DIR"
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B mongoose
.RI [ \-v | \-vv ]
.B sync
.BI \-\-work\-dir " DIR"
.RB [ \-\-cutover ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mongoose
migrates one NFS export to another from a single host. It scans the
source with an embedded parallel walker (nfs-walker), rewrites the scan
into canonical parquet shards, and copies the data over raw NFSv3 with
libnfs. After the initial copy it can resync incrementally while the
source stays live, finishing with a verified cutover. Everything lives
on local disk under one work directory: no external tools, no
coordinator, no S3.
.PP
Run as root: libnfs binds reserved ports for AUTH_SYS. NFSv3 only.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B prepare
Scan the source and build the local migration index (canonical shards
plus
.IR manifest.json )
under
.BR \-\-work\-dir .
Resumable: re-running picks up after the last completed stage.
.TP
.B copy
Copy using an index prepared under
.BR \-\-work\-dir .
Shards are processed sequentially; files within a shard copy
concurrently. Resumable at shard granularity (completed shards are
skipped).
.TP
.B run
.BR prepare ,
then
.BR copy .
.TP
.B sync
One converging resync pass: rescan the source, classify changes against
the previous pass, and copy only the delta. Repeat while the source is
live; finish with
.B \-\-cutover
after stopping source writers.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log verbosity. Default is compact: warnings plus mongoose's own stage
lines and progress ticks.
.B \-v
restores full INFO from the embedded walker/rewrite/mover engines;
.B \-vv
enables debug.
.BR RUST_LOG ,
when set, overrides this flag entirely.
.SH PREPARE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-src " URL"
Source export URL, e.g.\&
.IR nfs://source.example.com/export .
.TP
.BI \-\-dst " URL"
Destination export URL.
.TP
.BI \-\-source\-root " PATH"
Path inside the source export to migrate ("/" = whole export).
Default: /.
.TP
.BI \-\-dest\-root " PATH"
Path inside the destination export to copy into. Default: /.
.TP
.BI \-\-work\-dir " DIR"
Local directory holding this run's index, checkpoints, and results.
One migration per work dir.
.TP
.BI \-\-walker\-workers " N"
nfs-walker GETATTR workers. Default: 32.
.TP
.BI \-\-shard\-size\-mb " N"
Target size of each canonical parquet shard. Default: 512.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " GLOB"
Directory glob to exclude from the scan (repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-\-scan\-dir " DIR"
Use an existing nfs-walker output directory instead of scanning.
.TP
.BI \-\-run\-id " ID"
Run identifier recorded in
.I run.json
and
.IR manifest.json .
Default: run-<UTC timestamp>.
.TP
.B \-\-purge\-intermediates
Delete the raw walker scan output once the canonical shards are
committed. The scan is a pure intermediate that doubles the index
footprint; canonical shards and the manifest are always kept. A
.B \-\-scan\-dir
outside the work dir is never touched.
.SH COPY TUNING OPTIONS
Shared by
.BR copy ,
.BR run ,
and
.BR sync .
.TP
.BI \-\-nfs\-connections " N"
libnfs context pairs to pre-mount. Each pair costs two reserved ports;
~111 pairs is the observed per-host ceiling. Default: 32.
.TP
.BI \-\-inflight\-small " N"
Concurrent in-flight files < 1 MiB. Default: 256.
.TP
.BI \-\-inflight\-medium " N"
Concurrent in-flight files 1 MiB \(en 1 GiB. Default: 16.
.TP
.BI \-\-inflight\-large " N"
Concurrent in-flight files > 1 GiB. Default: 4.
.TP
.B \-\-use\-raw\-fh
Copy regular files through the raw NFSv3 filehandle fast path (~5 RPCs
per small file instead of ~60\(en80).
.TP
.B \-\-direct\-commit
Raw-FH path only: CREATE under the final name and skip the atomic
.I .partial
+ RENAME publish. Faster, but a crash can leave a torn file visible;
only safe while nothing consumes the destination.
.TP
.B \-\-bucketed\-async
Use the bucketed async libnfs pool for regular-file copies (opt-in; the
sync MultiPool remains the default).
.TP
.BI \-\-rpc\-timeout\-ms " N"
Per-RPC libnfs timeout in milliseconds (0 = libnfs default).
.SH SYNC OPTIONS
.B sync
accepts the copy tuning options above, plus
.BR \-\-walker\-workers ,
.BR \-\-shard\-size\-mb ,
.BR \-\-exclude ,
.BR \-\-scan\-dir ,
and
.B \-\-purge\-intermediates
(as in
.BR prepare ),
and:
.TP
.B \-\-cutover
Cutover verification: source writers must be stopped. Fails loudly if
the classifier finds any drift (new, dirty, pending, or deleted rows);
zero drift means the trees have converged.
.TP
.B \-\-cutover\-allow\-drift
With
.BR \-\-cutover :
copy the drift instead of failing on it.
.TP
.BI \-\-keep\-passes " N"
Completed pass dirs to retain (older ones are pruned after the baseline
advances). Default: 2.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success \(em including a deliberate SIGINT/SIGTERM stop (resume with
.BR "mongoose copy" ).
.TP
.B 1
Error (bad flags, missing index, unreachable export, corrupt shard).
.TP
.B 2
Copy completed but recorded per-file failures (see
.I failures/
in the work dir).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Overrides the
.B \-v
verbosity flag entirely (tracing-subscriber env-filter syntax).
.TP
.B LIBNFS_USE_ALL_RESERVED
Set to 1 by mongoose automatically so libnfs uses the full reserved
port range (without it,
.I /etc/services
name registrations throttle a host to ~55 context pairs). Export
.B LIBNFS_USE_ALL_RESERVED=0
to opt out.
.SH FILES
Work-dir layout:
.PP
.nf
<work-dir>/
  run.json                      run identity (sticky; a re-run with
                                different src/dst is refused)
  scan/attempt-NNNN/            nfs-walker output + progress log
  scan.json                     scan checkpoint
  canonical/part-NNNN.parquet   canonical shards
  rewrite.json                  rewrite checkpoint
  manifest.json                 local run plan
  progress.json                 copy progress + completed-shard list
  failures/part-NNNN.jsonl      per-file failures, per shard
  downgrades/part-NNNN.jsonl    per-file metadata downgrades, per shard
  passes/pass-NNNN/             resync pass state (classify results,
                                delta shards, deleted.jsonl)
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
Full migration in one shot:
.PP
.nf
mongoose run \\
  --src nfs://source.example.com/export \\
  --dst nfs://dest.example.com/export \\
  --work-dir /var/lib/mongoose/run-001 \\
  --nfs-connections 32 \\
  --use-raw-fh
.fi
.PP
Resync while the source stays live, then cut over:
.PP
.nf
mongoose sync --work-dir /var/lib/mongoose/run-001 --use-raw-fh
# ... stop source writers ...
mongoose sync --work-dir /var/lib/mongoose/run-001 --use-raw-fh
mongoose sync --work-dir /var/lib/mongoose/run-001 --cutover
.fi
.SH NOTES
Resync is scan-diff based: each pass is a full metadata rescan diffed
against the previous pass on (file_type, size, mtime, ctime), with
whole-file recopy on any mismatch. Deletions are detected and recorded
but never propagated to the destination. See the project README for the
full correctness posture and v1 limitations.
